  "slug": "association-adjusting-2e22",
  "summary": "New methods jointly model rare and common variants, relatives, and multi-phenotype interactions, alongside summary-statistic PRS and multi-tissue eQTL gene prioritization.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is statistical inference for genetic and omics association that models dependence or combines evidence types explicitly. PrediXSKAT embeds PrediXcan-predicted expression into the SKAT kernel to jointly test rare coding and common cis-regulatory variants. QT-RelCor supplies parametric and non-parametric tests for quantitative trait–disease association in clustered family data. GiMat extends multivariate kernel regression to SNP gene-gene interactions across multiple dichotomous phenotypes. LaMe estimates natural direct and indirect effects with joint latent mediation in high-dimensional systems. CAS-X integrates fine-mapped eQTL PIPs and allelic fold changes across five metabolic tissues for type 2 diabetes effector-gene prioritization, and a regularized ensemble PRS method works from GWAS summary statistics alone. The items are methodologically varied, and the evidence is mostly preprint-stage.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
